From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] ucode: handle a break of the handler

ucode 2026-10-18 adds STATUS_BREAK to uc_vm_status_t.  uc_vm_execute()
returns it when a break is requested while the program runs, which
only the remote debugger does.  The switch over the result of the
handler in uh_ucode_state_init() does not handle it, which fails the
build with -Werror=switch:

  ucode.c:295:9: error: enumeration value 'STATUS_BREAK' not handled
  in switch [-Werror=switch]

A break leaves the handler only partly run, so treat it as a failure,
as the ucode command line does outside the remote debug mode.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/ucode.c
+++ b/ucode.c
@@ -300,6 +300,10 @@
 		fprintf(stderr, "Error: The ucode handler invoked exit(%d)\n", exitcode);
 		exit(exitcode ? exitcode : 1);
 
+	case STATUS_BREAK:
+		fprintf(stderr, "Error: The ucode handler was interrupted\n");
+		exit(1);
+
 	case ERROR_COMPILE:
 		fprintf(stderr, "Error: Compilation error while executing ucode handler\n");
 		exit(1);
